# Shipped scripts, pinned (§3.3, defect 11).
#
# The encoding half of defect 11 is asserted by tests/test_shipped_script_encoding.py, which
# checks the bytes in the working tree. This file covers the way those bytes can change
# without anybody editing the file: a checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every LF to CRLF, which turns a shell script's shebang into `/usr/bin/env bash\r` and makes
# the kernel report "bad interpreter" about a file that plainly exists.
#
# eol=lf on the Unix scripts, eol=crlf on the Windows ones — each gets what its interpreter
# expects, on every machine, regardless of local git config.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.iss   text eol=crlf

# Test fixtures are compared byte for byte; never let git touch them.
*.pptx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.safetensors binary
